From de6b653f33581512bc5a34dd3ad5f0e3b424013a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: root <root@localhost>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 00:01:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(file): add --category-dir and --category-dir-scope

Port the category download feature of aria2-zero: a download whose file
name ends with a configured suffix is saved in a subdirectory of --dir.

  aria2c --category-dir="archive:.zip,.rar;text:.txt" http://host/film.zip

"--category-dir" takes one or more DIRECTORY:.SUFFIX,.SUFFIX rules; values
may repeat and rules may also be separated by ";" or a line break, so the
aria2-zero command line keeps working unchanged. Suffixes match the end of
the file name without regard to case, and a rule whose directory is
absolute or leaves --dir is dropped.

"--category-dir-scope" selects which names a rule may move, as in aria2-zero:
1 (default) names the URI or the server supplies, 2 names given with --out,
3 both. A name that already starts with its category stays put, so locating
the output twice never nests the file twice.

Deciding the output directory lives in Task::outputDirectory(), which the
HTTP/SFTP, ED2K and media tasks use before they join a name to --dir. RPC
reports the categorised path for a task that has not started yet, and a
"--dir" change carries the category to the new directory.
